--TEST--
A call through a `callable(static)` parameter needs an object of the class the call names, and a base-class call does not take a function for a subclass — `rule:statements/static-is-a-member-modifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Model {
    public function other(callable(static): bool $rule): bool {
        // A `Model` may not be the class the call named. This does not compile.
        return $rule(new Model());
    }

    public function stored(callable(static): bool $rule): bool {
        // A variable may contain any `Model`. This does not compile either.
        Model $model = new Model();
        return $rule($model);
    }

    public static function check(callable(static): bool $rule): bool {
        return true;
    }
}

class Order extends Model {
    public int $total = 0;
}

// `Model::check` needs a function that takes every `Model`.
// This function takes only `Order`, so the call does not compile.
Model::check(fn (Order $o): bool => $o->total > 0);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E1015]: this argument may not be the class the call named
%A
error[E1015]: this argument may not be the class the call named
%A
error[E0401]: expected `callable(Model): bool`, found `callable(Order): bool`
%A
   = help: This function takes only `Order`. Call the method on `Order`, for example `Order::check(...)`.

error: aborting due to 3 errors
